      <div class="faq-grid">
        <details class="faq-item reveal">
          <summary class="faq-question">What should I pack for Zanzibar's climate?</summary>
          <p class="faq-answer">Zanzibar has a tropical climate — hot and humid. Pack lightweight, breathable fabrics. Evenings can be cool, so bring a light jacket. The sun is strong year-round, so prioritize sun protection.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal delay-2">
          <summary class="faq-question">Do I need malaria tablets for Zanzibar?</summary>
          <p class="faq-answer">Malaria risk exists in Zanzibar. Consult a travel clinic before your trip for anti-malaria medication. Also pack insect repellent with DEET and sleep under a mosquito net.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal delay-3">
          <summary class="faq-question">What's the dress code in Zanzibar?</summary>
          <p class="faq-answer">Stone Town is conservative — cover shoulders and knees. Beaches are more relaxed — swimwear is fine on the beach. When in villages or religious sites, dress modestly.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item reveal delay-4">
          <summary class="faq-question">What toiletries should I bring?</summary>
          <p class="faq-answer">Bring sunscreen (reef-safe), insect repellent, basic first aid supplies, and any prescription medications. While toiletries are available in Zanzibar, they may be more expensive or have different formulations.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
